compilation/setup failure is not a property outcome.\",\n      \"No claim of core consensus disagreement or arbitrary-schedule progress.\"\n    ],\n    \"grounding_unresolved\": [],\n    \"review_limitations\": []\n  },\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n  ],\n  \"boundaries\": [\n    \"No guarantee that an arbitrary admitted invocation succeeds.\",\n    \"No global consensus agreement violation is asserted.\",\n    \"Crash persistence, reconfiguration, snapshotting and batching are outside this check.\",\n    \"A compilation/setup failure is not a property outcome.\",\n    \"No claim of core consensus disagreement or arbitrary-schedule progress.\"\n  ],\n  \"review_ids\": [],\n  \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n  \"correspondence\": null,\n  \"reviewed_complete\": false,\n  \"bounded_complete\": true,\n  \"confirmed\": false,\n  \"outcome\": \"violated\",\n  \"level\": \"implementation_test\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"c-notify-identity\",\n  \"claim_version\": 1,\n  \"framework_revision\": \"audit-products-v48\",\n  \"finding_ids\": {\n    \"notify-entry-identity\": \"fd4fed7ce7dc401694b93d2010b3d6e4\"\n  },\n  \"finding_id\": \"fd4fed7ce7dc401694b93d2010b3d6e4\"\n}\nclaims {\n  \"id\": \"c-notify-identity\",\n  \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n  \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n  \"description\": \"If append_notify completes successfully with an assigned log index, the decided entry at that index must be the entry submitted by that invocation, including when leadership changes between acceptance and notification. Timeout or Superseded is permitted instead of success.\",\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"description\": \"The captured async runtime over one valid three-node core configuration, distinct comparable entry payloads, no compaction or crash, and real core/runtime messages delivered by the caller. A partition may delay an old leader response while a different quorum elects a new leader and decides a different entry.\",\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Each node has a unique configured id and initially empty MemoryStorage.\",\n      \"Application supplies transport; no messages or state are fabricated or modified.\",\n      \"Success is interpreted at the one-based accepted index returned by the runtime; core read offset is index minus one.\"\n    ],\n    \"excluded\": [\n      \"No guarantee that an arbitrary admitted invocation succeeds.\",\n      \"No global consensus agreement violation is asserted.\",\n      \"Crash persistence, reconfiguration, snapshotting and batching are outside this check.\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": {}\n  },\n  \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-notify-contract\",\n    \"s-notify-errors\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n  \"candidate\": true,\n  \"grounding\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-runtime-assignment\",\n      \"s-runtime-forward\",\n      \"s-runtime-drain\"\n    ],\n    \"expectation_ids\": [\n      \"s-notify-contract\",\n      \"s-notify-errors\"\n    ],\n    \"binding_ids\": [\n      \"bind-notify-drain\"\n    ],\n    \"derivation\": \"The public method says append an entry and await its decided log index. The Superseded documentation permits stopping conservatively when a leader changes because the entry might still survive; this permits false-negative errors, not success for another value. Assignment records index and ballot at acceptance, while core consensus may replace unchosen values across ballots. Therefore success requires the requested entry, not solely a decided numeric position.\",\n    \"applicability\": \"Use the original caller invocation, its real tagged EntryId and real assignment; correlate successful response with the live decided log at the same origin.\",\n    \"unresolved\": [],\n    \"conflicts\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": [\n      \"Superseded or Timeout can satisfy the safety requirement without deciding the input.\",\n      \"If new leader retains the original value, successful notification is consistent with the requirement.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"version\": 1\n}\n{\n  \"description\": \"Test delayed old-leader assignment consumption after a replacement value is decided by a new quorum. The principal invocation is observed from its real TaggedProposal through Assigned, replacement decision at origin, and future completion plus live read. This is a safety implication, not a completion deadline test.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"c-notify-identity\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"bind-notify-drain\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"execution_package\": \"./omnipaxos_runtime\",\n    \"files\": {},\n    \"kind\": \"rust_test\",\n    \"source\": \"use std::{future::Future, time::Duration};\\nuse omnipaxos::{\\n    messages::{Message, async_runtime::AsyncRuntimeMsg},\\n    storage::{Entry, Snapshot}, util::LogEntry,\\n    ClusterConfig, OmniPaxosConfig, ServerConfig,\\n};\\nuse omnipaxos_runtime::{spawn_actor, AsyncRuntime, OmniPaxosHandle, RuntimeConfig};\\nuse omnipaxos_storage::memory_storage::MemoryStorage;\\n\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\\nstruct Value(u64);\\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]\\nstruct NoSnap;\\nimpl Snapshot<Value> for NoSnap {\\n    fn create(_: &[Value]) -> Self { Self }\\n    fn merge(&mut self, _: Self) {}\\n    fn use_snapshots() -> bool { false }\\n}\\nimpl Entry for Value { type Snapshot = NoSnap; }\\n\\n// Executor adapter only: the selected crate does not enable its optional TokioRuntime.\\nstruct Executor;\\nimpl AsyncRuntime for Executor {\\n    type JoinHandle = tokio::task::JoinHandle<()>;\\n    fn spawn<F: Future<Output=()> + Send + 'static>(f: F) -> Self::JoinHandle { tokio::spawn(f) }\\n    fn sleep(d: Duration) -> impl Future<Output=()> + Send + 'static { tokio::time::sleep(d) }\\n}\\ntype Handle = OmniPaxosHandle<Value>;\\n\\nfn node(pid: u64) -> Handle {\\n    let cfg = OmniPaxosConfig {\\n        cluster_config: ClusterConfig { configuration_id: 1, nodes: vec![1,2,3], ..Default::default() },\\n        server_config: ServerConfig {\\n            pid, batch_size: 1, election_tick_timeout: 100_000,\\n            resend_message_tick_timeout: 100_000, flush_batch_tick_timeout: 100_000,\\n            ..Default::default()\\n        },\\n    };\\n    let op = cfg.build(MemoryStorage::<Value>::default()).expect(\\\"valid cluster\\\");\\n    spawn_actor::<_,_,Executor>(op, RuntimeConfig {\\n        tick_period: Duration::from_millis(1), egress_period: Duration::from_millis(1),\\n        append_notify_timeout: Duration::from_secs(5), ..Default::default()\\n    })\\n}\\n\\n// Each outgoing queue is drained in order. Partitioned traffic is retained unchanged.\\nasync fn pump(nodes: &[Handle], isolate_one: bool, held: &mut Vec<Message<Value>>) {\\n    for n in nodes {\\n        let out = n.outgoing_messages();\\n        while let Ok(m) = out.try_recv() {\\n            if isolate_one && (m.get_sender() == 1 || m.get_receiver() == 1) {\\n                held.push(m);\\n            } else {\\n                nodes[(m.get_receiver()-1) as usize].handle_incoming(m).await;\\n            }\\n        }\\n        let events = n.subscribe_events();\\n        while events.try_recv().is_ok() {}\\n    }\\n    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(2)).await;\\n}\\nasync fn stable(nodes: &[Handle], ids: &[usize], leader: u64, isolated: bool, held: &mut Vec<Message<Value>>) {\\n    for _ in 0..500 {\\n        pump(nodes, isolated, held).await;\\n        let mut ready = true;\\n        for &i in ids { ready &= nodes[i].current_leader().await == Some((leader,true)); }\\n        if ready { return; }\\n    }\\n    panic!(\\\"leader preparation prerequisite not reached\\\");\\n}\\nfn payload(entries: Option<Vec<LogEntry<Value>>>) -> Option<u64> {\\n    match entries?.first()? { LogEntry::Decided(v) => Some(v.0), _ => None }\\n}\\n\\n#[test]\\nfn delayed_assignment_identity() {\\n    let rt = tokio::runtime::Builder::new_current_thread().enable_time().build().unwrap();\\n    rt.block_on(async {\\n        tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(20), async {\\n            let nodes = vec![node(1),node(2),node(3)];\\n            let mut held = Vec::new();\\n            nodes[0].try_become_leader().await;\\n            stable(&nodes, &[0,1,2], 1, false, &mut held).await;\\n            assert_eq!(nodes[2].decided_idx().await,0);\\n            println!(\\\"CA_EVENT {{\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"setup\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"old-write\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"old_leader\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"empty\\\\\\\":true}}\\\");\\n            let origin = nodes[2].clone();\\n            let pending = tokio::spawn(async move { origin.append_notify(Value(101)).await });\\n            // Pull the real TaggedProposal from origin and hand it to old leader.\\n            // All old-leader outbound messages are retained from this point onward.\\n            let mut tag = None;\\n            for _ in 0..500 {\\n                for (i,n) in nodes.iter().enumerate() {\\n                    let out = n.outgoing_messages();\\n                    while let Ok(m) = out.try_recv() {\\n                        if i == 2 {\\n                            if let Message::AsyncRuntime(a) = &m {\\n                                if let AsyncRuntimeMsg::TaggedProposal { entries } = &a.msg {\\n                                    assert_eq!(a.to,1);\\n                                    assert_eq!(entries.len(),1);\\n                                    assert_eq!(entries[0].1,Value(101));\\n                                    tag = Some(entries[0].0);\\n                                    println!(\\\"CA_EVENT {{\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"admitted\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"old-write\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"entry_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"input\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"old_leader\\\\\\\":1}}\\\",entries[0].0.0,entries[0].1.0);\\n                                    nodes[0].handle_incoming(m).await;\\n                                    continue;\\n                                }\\n                            }\\n                        }\\n                        held.push(m);\\n                    }\\n                }\\n                if tag.is_some() { break; }\\n                tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(2)).await;\\n            }\\n            let tag = tag.expect(\\\"real tagged invocation\\\");\\n            let mut assignment = None;\\n            for _ in 0..500 {\\n                let out = nodes[0].outgoing_messages();\\n                while let Ok(m) = out.try_recv() {\\n                    if let Message::AsyncRuntime(a) = &m {\\n                        if let AsyncRuntimeMsg::Assigned { ballot, entries } = &a.msg {\\n                            assert_eq!(a.to,3);\\n                            assert_eq!(entries.len(),1);\\n                            assert_eq!(entries[0].0,tag);\\n                            assignment = Some((entries[0].1,*ballot));\\n                        }\\n                    }\\n                    held.push(m);\\n                }\\n                if assignment.is_some() { break; }\\n                tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(2)).await;\\n            }\\n            let (assigned_idx, old_ballot) = assignment.expect(\\\"real old leader assignment\\\");\\n            assert_eq!(assigned_idx,1);\\n            assert_eq!(nodes[0].decided_idx().await,0);\\n            println!(\\\"CA_EVENT {{\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"assigned\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"old-write\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"entry_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"assigned_idx\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"ballot_n\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"old_decided\\\\\\\":0}}\\\",tag.0,assigned_idx,old_ballot.n);\\n            // Node 1 remains isolated; only 2 and 3 supply the new preparation quorum.\\n            nodes[1].try_become_leader().await;\\n            stable(&nodes, &[1,2], 2, true, &mut held).await;\\n            assert_eq!(nodes[1].decided_idx().await,0);\\n            nodes[1].append(Value(202)).await.expect(\\\"replacement admitted\\\");\\n            for _ in 0..500 {\\n                pump(&nodes,true,&mut held).await;\\n                if nodes[2].decided_idx().await >= assigned_idx { break; }\\n            }\\n            let replacement = payload(nodes[2].read_decided_suffix(assigned_idx-1).await).expect(\\\"replacement decided at origin\\\");\\n            assert_eq!(replacement,202);\\n            assert!(!pending.is_finished(),\\\"old request must still be pending before delayed assignment\\\");\\n            println!(\\\"CA_EVENT {{\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"replacement\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"old-write\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"entry_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"assigned_idx\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"new_leader\\\\\\\":2,\\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\":true}}\\\",tag.0,assigned_idx,replacement);\\n            // Release the old 1->3 stream in its original order, including the Assigned.\\n            // Other partitioned directions remain withheld. No message contents are edited.\\n            for m in held.drain(..) {\\n                if m.get_sender()==1 && m.get_receiver()==3 { nodes[2].handle_incoming(m).await; }\\n            }\\n            let result = tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(6),pending).await.expect(\\\"notification result available\\\").expect(\\\"caller task\\\");\\n            let (success,index,status) = match result {\\n                Ok(i) => (true,i,\\\"ok\\\"),\\n                Err(omnipaxos_runtime::AppendError::Superseded{log_entry_idx}) => (false,log_entry_idx,\\\"superseded\\\"),\\n                Err(omnipaxos_runtime::AppendError::Timeout) => (false,assigned_idx,\\\"timeout\\\"),\\n                Err(_) => (false,assigned_idx,\\\"other_error\\\"),\\n            };\\n            let value = if index > 0 { payload(nodes[2].read_decided_suffix(index-1).await) } else { None };\\n            let json_value = value.map(|v|v.to_string()).unwrap_or_else(||\\\"null\\\".into());\\n            println!(\\\"CA_EVENT {{\\\\\\\"event\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"notification\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"operation\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"old-write\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"entry_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"case\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"delayed_assignment\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"success\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"{}\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"returned_idx\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"actual_value\\\\\\\":{},\\\\\\\"decided_idx\\\\\\\":{}}}\\\",tag.0,success,status,index,json_value,nodes[2].decided_idx().await);\\n            drop(nodes);\\n            tokio::task::yield_now().await;\\n        }).await.expect(\\\"controlled history finished within harness bound\\\");\\n    });\\n}\\n\",\n    \"description\": \"Three public actors and a controlled in-process caller transport; generated messages are routed or retained unchanged. Bounded loops assert prerequisite reachability only.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"Executor adapter delegates spawn/sleep to Tokio without modifying actor semantics.\",\n      \"Transport withholds old leader links and later releases the original 1->3 stream; no protocol substitutions.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"setup\",\n        \"event\": \"setup\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"empty\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admission\",\n        \"event\": \"admitted\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"old_leader\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"setup.old_leader\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"assignment\",\n        \"event\": \"assigned\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"entry_id\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"admission.entry_id\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"old_decided\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 0,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"replacement\",\n        \"event\": \"replacement\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"entry_id\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"assignment.entry_id\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"assigned_idx\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"assignment.assigned_idx\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"new_leader\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 2,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"pending\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": true,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-runtime-assignment\",\n        \"s-runtime-forward\",\n        \"s-runtime-drain\",\n        \"s-runtime-loop\",\n        \"s-entry\",\n        \"s-follow\",\n        \"s-leader-start\",\n        \"s-memory\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"s-notify-contract\",\n        \"s-notify-errors\",\n        \"s-runtime-transport\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-notify-drain\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"Core build validates nodes 1,2,3 and default majority. Each actor starts with empty MemoryStorage. A standard Tokio-backed AsyncRuntime implements only spawn/sleep because the selected crate need not enable optional TokioRuntime. All target code is unmodified. Public try_become_leader elects node 1 and actual messages establish Accept on all nodes. The origin submits exactly one append_notify(101); the real TaggedProposal UUID and old leader Assigned are observed. Old leader outbound traffic is retained before delivery, so only node 1 accepts 101. Nodes 2 and 3 then run a real higher-ballot prepare/sync, admit 202 and decide it on their quorum. The 1->3 stream is released in FIFO order afterward. Runtime ticks continue every millisecond but core election/retry timeouts are 100000 ticks, avoiding unrelated automatic takeovers during the bounded history. Events are drained during message pumping; the small remaining suffix cannot fill the 1024-event channel. Handles are dropped and the test runtime ends after completion. No target manifests, locks, private fields or messages are edited.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"One valid configuration, distinct values, batch size one, no crash/compaction or state substitution; manually requested elections and per-link FIFO delayed messages.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"The pending request may conservatively report Superseded or Timeout, which is permitted.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"monitor-notify-identity\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"notify-entry-identity\",\n      \"event\": \"notification\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"bind-notify-drain\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"s-runtime-assignment\",\n          \"s-runtime-forward\",\n          \"s-runtime-drain\",\n          \"s-runtime-loop\",\n          \"s-entry\",\n          \"s-follow\",\n          \"s-leader-start\",\n          \"s-memory\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"s-notify-contract\",\n          \"s-notify-errors\",\n          \"s-runtime-transport\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"bind-notify-drain\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"Applies c-notify-identity to one real actor invocation. UUID is generated by the target and checked against its Assigned response. Numeric assignment is one-based accepted length; read_decided_suffix(index-1) observes the actual entry after completion. Success implies identity; Superseded/Timeout does not require success.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"One valid configuration, distinct values, batch size one, no crash/compaction or state substitution; manually requested elections and per-link FIFO delayed messages.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"The pending request may conservatively report Superseded or Timeout, which is permitted.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"notify-entry-identity\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_implication\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"case\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"delayed_assignment\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"actual_value\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"reference\": \"admission.input\"\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": {\n        \"field\": \"success\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"operation\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Successful completion must identify the original input value in the live decided log at the returned index; errors are permitted.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"A compilation/setup failure is not a property outcome.\",\n    \"No claim of core consensus disagreement or arbitrary-schedule progress.\"\n  ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
